Design details for BatchService:

```java
@Service
public class BatchService {
    // terminal statuses for batch closure
    private static final Set<String> TERMINAL = Set.of("SEALED","REJECTED","ROLLED_BACK","WINDOW_EXPIRED","DEPENDENCY_BLOCKED");

    @Transactional
    public BatchActionResult publish(PublishBatchRequest req) {
        List<BatchEdgeRef> edges = req.edges() == null ? List.of() : req.edges();
        // canonical sort members by requestId, edges by (pred, succ)
        // fingerprint
        String fp = fingerprint(req, edges);
        CutoverBatchPO existing = batchRepo.findBatch(req.batchId());
        if (existing != null) {
            if (!existing.getFingerprint().equals(fp)) throw new ConflictException(...);
            return new BatchActionResult(true, "同键同参重放，返回首次冻结结果", toView(existing));
        }
        // validate members unique
        List<BatchMemberRef> members = req.members();
        Set<String> ids = ...;
        if (ids.size() != members.size()) throw new BusinessRuleException("批次成员必须唯一");
        // edges validation
        for edge: 
            if (pred.equals(succ)) throw 422 自环
            if (!ids.contains(pred) || !ids.contains(succ)) throw 422 边端点须在批内
        // cycle detection (Kahn or DFS)
        if (hasCycle(ids, edges)) throw 422 环路
        // lock member request rows in sorted order
        Map<String, CutoverRequestPO> locked = repo.lockRequestsOrdered(List.copyOf(ids)) -> map
        for (member m : members) {
            CutoverRequestPO po = locked.get(m.requestId());
            if (po == null) throw new NotFoundException("割接申请不存在: " + m.requestId());
            if (!"APPROVED".equals(po.getStatus())) throw 422 "已批准但未开始" (已开始或未到批准)
            if (!po.getVersion().equals(m.expectedVersion())) throw 422 版本不符
            if (batchRepo.findActiveBatchId(m.requestId()) != null) throw 422 已属于未结束批次
        }
        // re-check batchId race: after locking member rows, re-find batch
        CutoverBatchPO afterLock = batchRepo.findBatch(req.batchId());
        if (afterLock != null) { same/diff fingerprint handling }

        // insert batch
        CutoverBatchPO batch = ...; version 1; status PUBLISHED; publishedAt; fingerprint fp
        batchRepo.insertBatch(batch);
        // insert members + bind
        for each member sorted by requestId:
            insert member (frozen version = po.getVersion(), window snapshot from po)
            po.setBatchId(batchId); po.setUpdatedAt(now); repo.updateMutable(po); // version+1
        // insert edges (sorted)
        return new BatchActionResult(false, "批次已发布...", toView(batch));
    }
}
```

Wait — ordering issue: insertBatch may throw DuplicateKeyException on concurrent same batchId. Handle like insertEvent: catch and compare fingerprint. But since we lock member rows first, two concurrent publishes with the same members serialize; with different members but same batchId, both could try insert → one gets DuplicateKeyException. Catch it → find winner → compare fingerprint → replay or 409.

Also deadlock: two publishes with overlapping member sets lock in sorted order → no deadlock.

Note: findActiveBatchId check — since we hold the request row lock, and any concurrent publish binding this request must also lock the row first, the check is race-free.

Validation order: 400 (bean validation) → 404 (not found) → 422 (business). Hmm — member uniqueness/format checks are 422 business per my earlier decision. But wait: should duplicate member be 400? The spec says "参数非法400、对象不存在404、业务拒绝422". Duplicate members is a semantic business rule ("成员必须唯一...整批拒绝") → 422. OK.

Order of checks: I'll do idempotency check first (existing batch → replay/409), then structural validation (unique/edges/cycle → 422), then lock rows, then 404/422 state checks. Hmm — but 404 should perhaps come before 422? If a member doesn't exist AND there's a cycle... ambiguous. I'll check existence first after locking (404), then status/version/batch-membership (422). Structural graph checks (422) before locking. Fine.

Cycle detection: Kahn's algorithm on member set with edges.

**Gating helper** for startExecution:

```java
/**
 * 返回 null 表示可启动；否则返回等待消息。
 * 调用方须已持有该申请行锁。
 */
public String batchGateMessage(CutoverRequestPO po) {
    if (po.getBatchId() == null) return null;
    CutoverBatchPO batch = batchRepo.findBatch(po.getBatchId());
    if (batch == null || !"PUBLISHED".equals(batch.getStatus())) return null;
    List<CutoverBatchEdgePO> edges = batchRepo.listEdges(po.getBatchId());
    List<String> preds = edges.stream().filter(e -> e.getSuccessor().equals(po.getRequestId())).map(predecessor).sorted().toList();
    if (preds.isEmpty()) return null;
    List<String> unsealed = new ArrayList<>();
    for (String p : preds) {
        CutoverRequestPO pred = repo.findRequest(p); // committed read
        if (pred == null || !"SEALED".equals(pred.getStatus())) unsealed.add(p);
    }
    if (unsealed.isEmpty()) return null;
    return "前置 " + unsealed + " 尚未验证通过并封板，等待中";
}
```

Hmm — should the gate lock predecessor rows? Analysis earlier: plain committed reads are fine because predecessor failure + propagation commit atomically. If predecessor is mid-rollback (uncommitted), we read old status (EXECUTING) → waiting. Safe.

But wait, there's a subtle race: predecessor commits SEALED... no issue. Predecessor commits ROLLED_BACK + propagation sets us DEPENDENCY_BLOCKED — but propagation needs OUR row lock, which startExecution holds. So propagation waits. Meanwhile we read predecessor status: if the predecessor's transaction hasn't committed, we see old status → waiting → release lock → propagation proceeds → blocks us. Consistent. If predecessor's transaction is waiting for our lock (propagation), it hasn't committed → we see old status → waiting. Then we commit (no change), propagation proceeds. Consistent — no deadlock since we don't wait on predecessor locks.

