Topological processing order: BFS by levels from the failed node. Since the subgraph reachable from failed node — process level by level; a node's direct preds that are reachable-and-blocked-in-this-run will have been processed in earlier levels (edges point pred→succ, BFS from source guarantees preds processed before succs... only for preds reachable from source. Direct preds NOT reachable from failed node can't be in blocking state due to this run; they might be in blocking state from earlier runs — read via findRequest).

